## Ship-bound drafts must pass `content-validator`

Apply these rules when drafting support communications. Use the `content-validator`
skill before completing a ship-bound draft, with the matching audience:

- Customer-facing Zendesk reply: `--audience customer`
- Zendesk internal note: `--audience internal-note`
- Slack message (any channel, DM, thread): `--audience slack`
- Engineering escalation issue body: `--audience escalation`
- `github/customer-feedback` issue or add-customer comment: `--audience feedback-issue`
- `github/helphub-knowledge-base` health-check PR review: `--audience health-check`

Run:

```bash
uv run --script ~/.agents/skills/content-validator/scripts/validate.py \
  --audience <audience> --file <path-to-draft> --fix --json
```

Do not declare a draft complete until `summary.blocks_unresolved` is `0` and every
`semantic_checklist` item has been addressed explicitly. If the skill or required
tools are unavailable, stop and report that validation is blocked rather than
skipping it. This check catches recurring formatting and drafting mistakes,
including em dashes, broken Zendesk formatting, wrong Slack channel scope,
file-path leaks, jargon, and unflagged inference.
