## Context hygiene on long ticket sessions

Keep large bundle dumps, ticket exports, and research output out of the main
conversation so long GHES ticket sessions remain usable.

- **Delegate large reads when supported.** Use a separate agent for bundle analysis, ticket-export mining, and multi-file research. Ask for conclusions rather than raw material.
- **Use `/ask` for side questions when supported.** It answers without adding to conversation history.
- **Prefer targeted searches and ranged reads over full-file mentions.** Active ticket exports can be very large. Use `rg` and `view_range`, or equivalent tools, instead of loading entire `zd{id}.md` files.
- **Use `ticket-resume` at around 60% context when available.** Reset from saved state instead of requesting a larger context window. See `~/.agents/skills/ticket-resume/SKILL.md`.
{{ end }}
## Skills

- **Source of truth:** `~/.agents/skills/` is the canonical location for all skills. Always look here first.
- **Symlinks:** Agent-specific skills paths may point to `~/.agents/skills/`. Resolve the symlink rather than treating it as a separate collection.
- When searching for skills, modifying skills, or referencing skill paths, always use `~/.agents/skills/` as the authoritative directory.
